525: free away from the selected rank-two cusp.  Indeed its equality
526: with an iterate of the contracting lift forces that iterate to
527: be zero by the norm inequality, and then forces the circle
528: element to be the identity.  This includes the whole \(I_8\)
529: neighbourhood, where translation permutes the components.  The
530: ordinary logarithmic cap is free as well.  At the single cusp
531: the primitive fan gives the one fixed rational curve with normal
532: weights \((-1,+1)\).  The orbit-pair argument P3F.7 therefore
533: applies to this proved sphere: its quotient is the standard
534: \((S^5,S^2)\), and its Euler line has positive meridian one.
535: 
536: The gamma circle over the base has the one ordinary clutch of
537: degree one, so its total space is the standard Hopf \(S^3\).
538: For precision, in the two standard Hopf charts the normalized
539: sections \((1,t)/\sqrt{1+|t|^2}\) and
540: \((1/t,1)/\sqrt{1+|1/t|^2}\) have angular coordinates related
541: by \(\theta_\infty=\theta_0+\arg t\), exactly the clutch
542: above.  A regular Hopf binding has a complex-oriented disc page
543: whose projection to \(\mathbf P^1\) has degree one.  Its inverse
544: image in the actual orbit is the elliptic page \(V\), with
545: boundary \(T^3\); its regular cap is the displayed rational
546: elliptic surface \(S\).  The affine origin obstruction on the
547: disc with marked singular values vanishes by the free-meridian
548: cochain argument of P3F.10.  Thus this comparison is with the
549: actual page, including the retained \(I_8\), rather than with
550: an unrelated elliptic surface.
551: 
552: The actual circle line restricts to \(M=8G-O\), up to a base
553: pullback, by its fibrewise Picard point.  At \(I_8\) both lines
554: have multidegree zero, so the same normalized fibrewise comparison
555: extends across its cycle of components.  On the base with boundary
556: the pullback is topologically trivial.  Therefore the actual
557: relative page invariants are
558: 
559: \[
560:  s_\delta=M^2=-2-2(3)=-8,
561:  \qquad p_{\rm rel}=3\sigma(S)=-24.
562: \]
563: 
564: Near the selected \(I_1\) the source translation is in the smooth
565: identity component.  The product coordinate of P3F.9 and the real
566: phase-preserving compression of P3K.6 consequently apply with
567: page degree \(d=1\).  The page phase can be chosen to avoid the
568: short gamma arc of that compression.  Its exact graph boundary,
569: integral Euler-line restriction, and oriented complement bordism
570: are therefore the ones proved in P3K.6–7.  The angular computation
571: above identifies this bordism with the actual positive scalar
572: return.  With the two orientation reversals of P3K.7 retained,
573: 
574: \[
575:  A=\frac{12s_\delta-p_{\rm rel}}{24}
576:    =\frac{-96+24}{24}=-3.
577: \]
578: 
579: The typed Hopf transfer and Eells--Kuiper normalization P3F.22 give
580: the asserted oriented class \(25\).  Pullback by
581: \(\lambda=z^n\) is a proper holomorphic family on the punctured
582: disc and its positive loop is exactly the \(n\)-fold iterate.
583: The classes \(-3n\pmod{28}\), for positive \(n\), exhaust
584: \(\mathbf Z/28\).  The mapping-torus obstruction P3F.24 applies
585: to each nonzero class and to both spin structures.  This proves
586: all the assertions of the statement.  **End of proof.**
